# The book-to-skill tree is byte-pinned to upstream commit c6bc1b79 and every
# path's SHA-256 is recorded in tests/codex_skills/test_upstream_manifest.py.
#
# The pinned blobs are stored LF-only, and this repository sets
# core.autocrlf=true. Without an attribute here Git would rewrite every one of
# them to CRLF on checkout — `git ls-files --eol` reports `i/lf w/crlf` for any
# unpinned text file in this repo, against `i/lf w/lf` for these. All nineteen
# recorded digests would stop matching at once, and re-deploying from such a
# checkout would ship bytes that are not the audited ones.
#
# `-text` freezes the bytes exactly as they were audited, in both directions.
# `-whitespace` stops `git diff --check`, `git apply --whitespace=fix`, and
# whitespace-linting hooks from reporting — or silently repairing — upstream's
# own formatting inside a tree nobody here is allowed to edit.
#
# Git reads attributes from the index during checkout, so removing this file
# from the working tree does not relax the pin; it has to be removed from a
# commit before it stops applying.
book-to-skill/** -text -whitespace
